BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:thasos-kallirachi-transfiguration-panigiri-old-kallirachi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270806
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270807
SUMMARY:Transfiguration panigiri\, Old Kallirachi
LOCATION:Kallirachi\, Thasos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The hill village of (old) Kallirachi on the west coast celebrates the Transfiguration on 6 August with a feast organised by its cultural association\, part of the municipal summer programme. The next night (7 August) Skala Kallirachi below holds its harbour festival with a big-name Greek singer. Prinos\, further north\, has a traditional celebration with Thracian-style music around 16 August.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/thasos/#kallirachi-transfiguration-panigiri-old-kallirachi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/thasos/#kallirachi-transfiguration-panigiri-old-kallirachi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:heraklion-agios-myronas-panigiri-of-agios-myron-agios-myronas-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270807
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270809
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Myron\, Agios Myronas
LOCATION:Agios Myronas\, Crete (Heraklion)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:One of the largest panigiria in Crete: the Malevizi village where the saint lived holds a hierarchical vespers and an all-night liturgy on 7 August\, the procession of his relics on the 8th\, and two nights of Cretan music in the main square (Kounalis brothers and Kallergis brothers in 2026). Pilgrims queue for the saint's tomb and the holy-water cave under the church. The village is 20 minutes from Heraklion\; parking is on the approach road\, so come early.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#agios-myronas-panigiri-of-agios-myron-agios-myronas
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#agios-myronas-panigiri-of-agios-myron-agios-myronas
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-mandria-panigiri-of-agios-triantafyllos-mandria-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270808
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270809
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Triantafyllos\, Mandria
LOCATION:Mandria\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:A small Raches-area village feast on 8 August\, with Nikos Fakaros and the Musicarous playing in 2026. Typical west-Ikaria format: tables in the square\, goat and wine from the association\, dancing well past midnight. Kossoikia (Evdilos side) keeps the same saint the same night.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#mandria-panigiri-of-agios-triantafyllos-mandria
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#mandria-panigiri-of-agios-triantafyllos-mandria
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lasithi-achladia-olive-oil-festival-achladia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270809
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270810
SUMMARY:Olive Oil Festival\, Achladia
LOCATION:Achladia\, Crete (Lasithi)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The olive village south of Sitia celebrates its oil on the evening of 9 August with dishes cooked in the new-season Sitia PDO oil and a Cretan kompania (Petros Maroulis in 2025)\, part of the Kornaria programme. Twenty minutes from Sitia\; the Minoan villa of Achladia is next to the village if you come early.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lasithi/#achladia-olive-oil-festival-achladia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lasithi/#achladia-olive-oil-festival-achladia
