BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:corfu-corfu-town-litany-of-agios-spyridon-for-the-1716-siege-corfu-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270812
SUMMARY:Litany of Agios Spyridon for the 1716 siege\, Corfu town
LOCATION:Corfu town\, Corfu\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:One of four annual processions of the relics of Saint Spyridon\, patron of Corfu. The casket is carried through the old town accompanied by all three philharmonic orchestras. The August one commemorates deliverance from a 1716 Ottoman siege.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#corfu-town-litany-of-agios-spyridon-for-the-1716-siege-corfu
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#corfu-town-litany-of-agios-spyridon-for-the-1716-siege-corfu
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-amalou-panigiri-of-agioi-evlampios-evlampia-amalou-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270811
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agioi Evlampios & Evlampia\, Amalou
LOCATION:Amalou\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Amalou\, a tiny stone village on the wild west coast below Vrakades\, hosts a 'big panigiri' on 10 August with the Zevkalides. It is one of the most atmospheric spots on the island to dance\, but the access road is rough and there is almost no parking\; go with one car per group. Faros (near the airport) and Steli/Platani celebrate the same night.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#amalou-panigiri-of-agioi-evlampios-evlampia-amalou
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#amalou-panigiri-of-agioi-evlampios-evlampia-amalou
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-faros-panigiri-of-faros-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270811
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Faros
LOCATION:Faros\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The beach village of Faros at the eastern tip\, next to the airport\, holds its panigiri on 10 August with the Ikariotiki Kompania. Handy if you are staying in Agios Kirykos or arriving by plane: flat\, by the sea\, easy parking along the beach road. Food and wine from the village association\, dancing till late.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#faros-panigiri-of-faros
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#faros-panigiri-of-faros
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lefkada-lazarata-feast-of-agios-spyridon-lazarata-and-karya-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270812
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Spyridon\, Lazarata and Karya
LOCATION:Lazarata\, Lefkada\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The 11 August miracle of Agios Spyridon is a big day in the Sfakiotes villages: in Lazarata there is vespers with artoklasia on the 10th\, liturgy on the morning of the 11th and an evening procession of the icon through the village to the square\, while neighbouring Karya carries its own reliquary under the plane trees the same morning. Village tavernas and the squares fill up afterwards\; the lay panigiri on Karya's square has traditionally followed the same weekend.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lefkada/#lazarata-feast-of-agios-spyridon-lazarata-and-karya
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lefkada/#lazarata-feast-of-agios-spyridon-lazarata-and-karya
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-avlaki-fishermen-s-panigiri-psaropanigiro-avlaki-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270811
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270812
SUMMARY:Fishermen's panigiri (psaropanigiro)\, Avlaki
LOCATION:Avlaki\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The fishing hamlet of Avlaki near Karavostamo serves fish instead of goat at its psaropanigiro on the harbour. Sources disagree on the date: the 2026 island list gives 11 August (Agios Efplous / Agios Fanourios)\, while older lists put it on 27 August for Agios Fanourios\, so check the ikariaki.gr calendar in the week before. Either way it is small\, cheap and on the water.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#avlaki-fishermen-s-panigiri-psaropanigiro-avlaki
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#avlaki-fishermen-s-panigiri-psaropanigiro-avlaki
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-manganitis-summer-panigiri-of-manganitis-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270813
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270814
SUMMARY:Summer panigiri of Manganitis
LOCATION:Manganitis\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Manganitis\, the cliff-hung fishing village on the south coast reached through the tunnel road\, has its summer panigiri on 13 August\, run by the residents' association 'To Kavaki' (Nikos Fakaros's orchestra in 2019\, the Periichou ensemble with Panagiotis Choutras in 2026). It is not tied to a saint\, just the village's night: tables around the harbour\, island songs and dancing until late. Fles near Evdilos holds a wine feast the same night.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#manganitis-summer-panigiri-of-manganitis
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#manganitis-summer-panigiri-of-manganitis
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:agistri-metochi-panigiri-of-panagia-15-august-metochi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia (15 August)\, Metochi
LOCATION:Metochi\, Agistri\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The little church of Panagia in the hamlet of Metochi above Megalochori has the island's Dekapentavgoustos celebration\, reached on foot along the trail\; the whole island turns out and the tavernas in Megalochori take the overflow. Book a room for that weekend\, Agistri fills with Athenians.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/agistri/#metochi-panigiri-of-panagia-15-august-metochi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/agistri/#metochi-panigiri-of-panagia-15-august-metochi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:amorgos-langada-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-epanochoriani-langada-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri of Panagia Epanochoriani\, Langada
LOCATION:Langada\, Amorgos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Langada above Aegiali celebrates 15 August at the church of Panagia Epanochoriani (Panochoriani) up the hill\; older pilgrims still ride donkeys up\, and afterwards the village serves patatato and xydato with plenty of rakomelo\, violins and dancing in the square through the night. The Archaia Arkesini association in Kato Meria holds a traditional food-and-dance evening the same day.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#langada-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-epanochoriani-langada
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#langada-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-epanochoriani-langada
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:andros-korthi-dormition-panigiri-korthi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri\, Korthi
LOCATION:Korthi\, Andros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Korthi bay in the south is the island's best-known 15 August panigiri: liturgy and procession\, then froutalia and soumada (almond cordial) in the square with island instruments and dancing. The same night Livadia and Makrotantalo in the north\, and Ammolos and Pano Katakoilos hold their own glentia\, and in Chora the seaside chapel of Panagia Thalassini celebrates.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/andros/#korthi-dormition-panigiri-korthi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/andros/#korthi-dormition-panigiri-korthi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:astypalaia-chora-panigiri-of-panagia-portaitissa-chora-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Portaitissa\, Chora
LOCATION:Chora\, Astypalaia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The big island festival at the Portaitissa church just below the castle. Procession\, music\, lamb on the spit.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/astypalaia/#chora-panigiri-of-panagia-portaitissa-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/astypalaia/#chora-panigiri-of-panagia-portaitissa-chora
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:chania-chrysoskalitissa-dormition-pilgrimage-at-chrysoskalitissa-mo-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition pilgrimage at Chrysoskalitissa Monastery
LOCATION:Chrysoskalitissa\, Crete (Chania)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The white monastery on its rock five kilometres from Elafonisi is the big Dormition pilgrimage of western Chania: vespers on the 14th with a Cretan glenti below the monastery (Kounalis and Georgiladakis in 2026)\, then the morning liturgy on the 15th. The approach road is single-track and fills with cars\, so come before sunset and expect to walk the last stretch.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chania/#chrysoskalitissa-dormition-pilgrimage-at-chrysoskalitissa-mo
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chania/#chrysoskalitissa-dormition-pilgrimage-at-chrysoskalitissa-mo
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:chania-meskla-kreatotourta-meat-pie-festival-for-the-dormition-mesk-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Kreatotourta (meat pie) festival for the Dormition\, Meskla
LOCATION:Meskla\, Crete (Chania)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the eve of the Dormition the village at the foot of the White Mountains bakes its kreatotourta\, the Chania meat-and-cheese pie\, and serves it with music in the square (Nikos Pontikakis played 2026). It is one of a dozen panigiria in Kydonia that night\, so it is not overrun. The road up from Fournes is narrow\; leave the car below the church.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chania/#meskla-kreatotourta-meat-pie-festival-for-the-dormition-mesk
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chania/#meskla-kreatotourta-meat-pie-festival-for-the-dormition-mesk
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:chania-fres-panigiri-of-the-dormition-fres-and-litsarda-apokoronas-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition\, Fres and Litsarda (Apokoronas)
LOCATION:Fres\, Crete (Chania)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Apokoronas plateau is the densest panigiri zone in Chania on 14–15 August: Fres\, Litsarda\, Pemonia\, Alikampos and Kefalas all hold two-night feasts with lyra-and-laouto kompanies (Pantermakis\, Karkanis\, Kontaros\, Pontikakis in 2026). Villages are a few minutes apart\, so people move between squares\; dancing goes on until dawn. Book a taverna table or bring cash for the syllogos food stall.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chania/#fres-panigiri-of-the-dormition-fres-and-litsarda-apokoronas
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chania/#fres-panigiri-of-the-dormition-fres-and-litsarda-apokoronas
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:chios-sidirounta-eve-of-the-dormition-panigiri-sidirounta-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Eve-of-the-Dormition panigiri\, Sidirounta
LOCATION:Sidirounta\, Chios\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Sidirounta\, a hillside village on the west coast road to Volissos with a wide view over the Aegean\, holds a big open-air panigiri on the night of 14 August from 22:00 with a live orchestra (Makrokanis-Tzikas in 2026)\, free entry and food from the village taverna. Good stop if you are heading to the western beaches\; the road back to town is dark and winding.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chios/#sidirounta-eve-of-the-dormition-panigiri-sidirounta
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chios/#sidirounta-eve-of-the-dormition-panigiri-sidirounta
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:corfu-peroulades-panigiri-of-the-dormition-peroulades-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition\, Peroulades
LOCATION:Peroulades\, Corfu\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The village above the Loggas cliffs runs a two-night panigiri on 14 and 15 August organised by the local football club\, with well-known Corfiot folk musicians (the Skolarikis family in 2025) and dancing in the square\; food and wine from the club. Combine with sunset at Loggas beach\, then walk up\; parking in the village is tight.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#peroulades-panigiri-of-the-dormition-peroulades
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#peroulades-panigiri-of-the-dormition-peroulades
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:donousa-stavros-dormition-panigiri-stavros-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri\, Stavros
LOCATION:Stavros\, Donousa\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The port village of Stavros hosts Donousa's biggest feast on 14-15 August: liturgy\, then patatato (goat with potatoes) and other local dishes served to everyone\, with live traditional music and dancing on the square until late. The island has a handful of rooms and one ferry a day\; book both months ahead.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/donousa/#stavros-dormition-panigiri-stavros
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/donousa/#stavros-dormition-panigiri-stavros
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:elafonisos-kato-nisi-panigiri-of-panagia-katonisiotissa-kato-nisi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Katonisiotissa\, Kato Nisi
LOCATION:Kato Nisi\, Elafonisos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The island's big day: an all-night vigil at the church of Panagia Katonisiotissa in Kato Nisi on the 14th\, while the young people light fires on the Panagia beach below and sing and dance until dawn\; liturgy on the morning of the 15th\, then a popular panigiri with the island's women's and children's dance groups in the afternoon. Boats used to bring crowds from Mani and Kythira\; today it is islanders and summer visitors\, and the beach bonfire is the thing to see.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/elafonisos/#kato-nisi-panigiri-of-panagia-katonisiotissa-kato-nisi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/elafonisos/#kato-nisi-panigiri-of-panagia-katonisiotissa-kato-nisi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:evia-central-oxylithos-kymi-stifado-of-the-panagia-15-august-oxylithos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Stifado of the Panagia (15 August)\, Oxylithos
LOCATION:Oxylithos (Kymi)\, Evia (Central)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The most famous Dekapentavgoustos custom in Evia: at the church of Panagia Petriotissa in Oxylithos\, near Kymi\, the bell rings on the afternoon of 14 August\, fires are lit under dozens (locally 'over 200') of cauldrons and volunteers stew beef with tons of onions all night\, nobody tasting\, until it is blessed and served free to everyone after the liturgy on the 15th. Neighbouring Kalimeriani and Potamia keep the same custom. Thousands come from Athens\; sleep in Kymi or Platana and get there before the 8 am liturgy.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-central/#oxylithos-kymi-stifado-of-the-panagia-15-august-oxylithos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-central/#oxylithos-kymi-stifado-of-the-panagia-15-august-oxylithos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:evia-north-papades-panigiri-of-panagia-eve-of-15-august-papades-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia (eve of 15 August)\, Papades
LOCATION:Papades\, Evia (North)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The village of Papades\, in the hills between Agia Anna and Vasilika\, throws its Panagia panigiri in the square on the night of 14 August with a live orchestra\, organised by the local cultural society and listed by the municipality. Small\, cheap and genuinely local\; the coast villages are 15 minutes away for a bed.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-north/#papades-panigiri-of-panagia-eve-of-15-august-papades
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-north/#papades-panigiri-of-panagia-eve-of-15-august-papades
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:folegandros-chora-dormition-panigiri-at-panagia-chora-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri at Panagia\, Chora
LOCATION:Chora\, Folegandros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The white church of Panagia on the hill above Chora — the island's landmark — celebrates the Dormition with vespers on the evening of 14 August\, a procession\, and a glenti with violin and laouto in the Chora squares\, followed by liturgy on the 15th. The island is at capacity that week\; the zig-zag path up to the church is unlit\, so bring a torch.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/folegandros/#chora-dormition-panigiri-at-panagia-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/folegandros/#chora-dormition-panigiri-at-panagia-chora
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:halki-nimborio-panigiri-of-panagia-nimborio-panagia-choriatis-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia\, Nimborio (Panagia Choriatis)
LOCATION:Nimborio\, Halki\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Halki's Dormition is a two-part affair: liturgy on the 15th at the restored church of Panagia Choriatis up in the old village of Chorio\, and on the evening of the 14th and 15th a glendi with Dodecanese musicians on the Nimborio harbour front. Everything is a five-minute walk in Nimborio\; the Chorio church is a 3 km walk or taxi ride uphill.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/halki/#nimborio-panigiri-of-panagia-nimborio-panagia-choriatis
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/halki/#nimborio-panigiri-of-panagia-nimborio-panagia-choriatis
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:heraklion-ano-archanes-panigiri-of-panagia-faneromeni-ano-archanes-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Faneromeni\, Ano Archanes
LOCATION:Ano Archanes\, Crete (Heraklion)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Archanes keeps the Dormition at its church of Panagia Faneromeni: festive vespers with a Byzantine choir and artoklasia on the 14th\, liturgy from 7 am on the 15th\, and a glenti in the restored village square with the local wine flowing. The village is 15 km from Heraklion with plenty of tavernas\; reserve a table for the evening of the 14th.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#ano-archanes-panigiri-of-panagia-faneromeni-ano-archanes
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#ano-archanes-panigiri-of-panagia-faneromeni-ano-archanes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hydra-hydra-town-dekapentavgoustos-at-the-cathedral-of-the-panagia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dekapentavgoustos at the Cathedral of the Panagia\, Hydra Town
LOCATION:Hydra Town\, Hydra\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The 17th-century monastery-cathedral of the Koimisis on the harbour front is Hydra's main church\, so 15 August is its name day: vespers on the 14th\, liturgy and a procession of the icon through the port streets on the 15th\, with the whole island in its best clothes. Peak season\, no cars and every room taken\, so book months ahead if you want to be there.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/hydra/#hydra-town-dekapentavgoustos-at-the-cathedral-of-the-panagia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/hydra/#hydra-town-dekapentavgoustos-at-the-cathedral-of-the-panagia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ios-chora-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-gremiotissa-chora-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri of Panagia Gremiotissa\, Chora
LOCATION:Chora\, Ios\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Ios's biggest feast — the Dormition\, celebrated at the cliff-edge church of Panagia Gremiotissa crowning Chora. Morning liturgy\, then the whole village tips into eating\, dancing and music until dawn\, with fireworks over the harbour. The walk up through the white lanes at dusk is half the experience.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ios/#chora-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-gremiotissa-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ios/#chora-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-gremiotissa-chora
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:iraklia-panagia-chora-dormition-panigiri-panagia-village-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri\, Panagia village
LOCATION:Panagia (Chora)\, Iraklia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The upper village of Panagia celebrates its church on 14-15 August with a vigil\, the liturgy\, and a panigiri in the church courtyard: goat and patatato cooked by the community\, wine\, and violins until late\, with boats bringing people over from Schinoussa and Naxos. Walk up from the port (30 minutes) or take the minibus.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/iraklia/#panagia-chora-dormition-panigiri-panagia-village
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/iraklia/#panagia-chora-dormition-panigiri-panagia-village
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ithaca-anogi-panigiri-of-the-dormition-eve-anogi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition eve\, Anogi
LOCATION:Anogi\, Ithaca\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 14 August the mountain hamlet of Anogi\, home to the byzantine church of the Dormition with its frescoes and Venetian bell tower\, hosts a panigiri in the church courtyard: the villagers roast meat and pour their own wine\, and there is dancing until sunrise. Ithacans call it the most fun night of the summer\; the drive from Stavros is short but winding\, so share a car.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ithaca/#anogi-panigiri-of-the-dormition-eve-anogi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ithaca/#anogi-panigiri-of-the-dormition-eve-anogi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kalamos-kefali-porto-leone-feast-of-the-dormition-at-kefali-kalamos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Feast of the Dormition at Kefali\, Kalamos
LOCATION:Kefali (Porto Leone)\, Kalamos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The abandoned village of Kefali at Kalamos's southern cape comes alive once a year: festive vespers with artoklasia at 7:30pm on 14 August and a hierarchical liturgy on the morning of the 15th at the church of Agioi Anargyroi\, with the Metropolitan of Lefkada\, pilgrims arriving by boat from Mytikas and Kalamos village\, and a treat offered afterwards. There is no road\; arrange a boat from Kalamos port or Mytikas the day before.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kalamos/#kefali-porto-leone-feast-of-the-dormition-at-kefali-kalamos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kalamos/#kefali-porto-leone-feast-of-the-dormition-at-kefali-kalamos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kalymnos-arginonta-panigiri-of-panagia-galatiani-arginonta-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Galatiani\, Arginonta
LOCATION:Arginonta\, Kalymnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The alternative 15 August on Kalymnos\, for the Masouri/Arginonta side of the island: the chapel of Panagia Galatiani in the Arginonta valley has a vigil and then a glendi with local musicians\, an easier option than the climb to Kyra Psili and popular with the climbing crowd staying in Masouri. Ten minutes from Masouri by scooter.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kalymnos/#arginonta-panigiri-of-panagia-galatiani-arginonta
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kalymnos/#arginonta-panigiri-of-panagia-galatiani-arginonta
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kalymnos-vathy-panigiri-of-panagia-kyra-psili-vathy-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Kyra Psili\, Vathy
LOCATION:Vathy\, Kalymnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The island's main Dormition feast is at the cliff monastery of Kyra Psili above the Vathy valley: pilgrims walk up in the evening of the 14th with mats and blankets\, the vigil starts around 9-10 pm\, and afterwards there is tsambouna-and-laouto music\, dancing and food stalls until morning. Wear proper shoes for the path and bring water\; cars stop well below the monastery.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kalymnos/#vathy-panigiri-of-panagia-kyra-psili-vathy
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kalymnos/#vathy-panigiri-of-panagia-kyra-psili-vathy
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:karpathos-olympos-panigiri-of-panagia-olympos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270817
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia\, Olympos
LOCATION:Olympos\, Karpathos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Three-day panigiria in Olympos and Othos villages with traditional dancing.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/karpathos/#olympos-panigiri-of-panagia-olympos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/karpathos/#olympos-panigiri-of-panagia-olympos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kasos-panagia-panigiri-of-pera-panagia-panagia-village-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Pera Panagia\, Panagia village
LOCATION:Panagia\, Kasos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The biggest day of the Kasos year: the whole island\, plus 2\,000-odd diaspora Kasiots\, gathers at the church in the village of Panagia. Kasiot dolmadakia (tiny stuffed vine leaves)\, stewed meat with cinnamon pilaf and fried potatoes are served free\, and sousta and zervos dancing to lyra and laouto runs from midday to dawn. Ferries and the tiny plane fill up\; book in June.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kasos/#panagia-panigiri-of-pera-panagia-panagia-village
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kasos/#panagia-panigiri-of-pera-panagia-panagia-village
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kefalonia-markopoulo-panagia-fidousa-the-snakes-of-the-virgin-markopou-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panagia Fidousa (the snakes of the Virgin)\, Markopoulo
LOCATION:Markopoulo\, Kefalonia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Between 6 and 15 August small harmless snakes with a cross-like mark appear around the church of the Dormition in Markopoulo\, above Katelios\, and are handled by the faithful during the vespers of the 14th and the liturgy of the 15th\; years when they fail to show (1940\, 1953) are remembered as bad omens. It is a pilgrimage\, not a panigiri\, and the church is tiny\, so arrive by 6pm on the 14th if you want to get inside.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kefalonia/#markopoulo-panagia-fidousa-the-snakes-of-the-virgin-markopou
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kefalonia/#markopoulo-panagia-fidousa-the-snakes-of-the-virgin-markopou
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kefalonia-simotata-livathos-panigiri-of-the-dormition-simotata-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition\, Simotata
LOCATION:Simotata (Livathos)\, Kefalonia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Livathos village of Simotata keeps 15 August the traditional way: vespers\, then from 8pm on the 14th a village panigiri in the square with live music\, food from the cultural association and dancing. Ten minutes from the airport and the Lassi hotels\, so easy to reach\; the same night Agkonas in Thinia has a panigiri with the Pavlatos orchestra if you prefer the west.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kefalonia/#simotata-livathos-panigiri-of-the-dormition-simotata
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kefalonia/#simotata-livathos-panigiri-of-the-dormition-simotata
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kimolos-chorio-dormition-panigiri-chorio-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri\, Chorio
LOCATION:Chorio\, Kimolos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kimolos keeps Dekapentavgoustos simply: vespers on the 14th\, liturgy and a procession of the icon through the lanes of Chorio on the 15th\, and a traditional glenti with violin and laouto in the village. It coincides with the peak of the summer 'Cultural August' events run by the Athens-based Kimolian associations\, so the island is at its fullest — the Milos–Kimolos ferry from Pollonia gets very busy those days.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kimolos/#chorio-dormition-panigiri-chorio
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kimolos/#chorio-dormition-panigiri-chorio
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kos-kefalos-panigiri-of-panagia-styliotis-kefalos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia (Styliotis)\, Kefalos
LOCATION:Kefalos\, Kos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The biggest village panigiri on Kos: the shepherds of Kefalos\, the old capital at the far west\, cook boiled goat with pilaf in huge cauldrons and serve it free after the liturgy on the 15th\, with dancing to island music on the square the night before and after. Kefalos also runs a fish festival in the first half of August. Parking in the village is tight\; use the road below and walk up.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kos/#kefalos-panigiri-of-panagia-styliotis-kefalos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kos/#kefalos-panigiri-of-panagia-styliotis-kefalos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kythnos-kanala-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-kanala-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri of Panagia Kanala
LOCATION:Kanala\, Kythnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The island's patroness\, whose icon was found floating in the channel between Kythnos and Serifos\, draws pilgrims from all over the Aegean: vespers on 14 August at the pine-shaded shrine above Kanala beach\, an all-night glenti with violin and laouto\, and on the 15th a liturgy and a re-enactment of the icon's finding with a procession down to the little harbour. Rooms in Kanala sell out weeks ahead\; most people stay in Dryopida or Chora and drive over.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#kanala-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-kanala
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#kanala-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-kanala
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lefkada-kalamitsi-panigiri-of-the-dormition-kalamitsi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition\, Kalamitsi
LOCATION:Kalamitsi\, Lefkada\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kalamitsi\, the hill village above Kathisma beach\, runs a two-night panigiri on 14 and 15 August in the old school yard\, organised by the Neromylos cultural society: live folk orchestra\, souvlaki and local wine\, dancing until late. It is the closest proper village panigiri to the west-coast beaches\; the road up from Kathisma is steep and parking is on the roadside.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lefkada/#kalamitsi-panigiri-of-the-dormition-kalamitsi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lefkada/#kalamitsi-panigiri-of-the-dormition-kalamitsi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lemnos-propouli-feast-of-panagia-tis-trygis-propouli-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270817
SUMMARY:Feast of Panagia tis Trygis\, Propouli
LOCATION:Propouli\, Lemnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Athonite metochi of Panagia tis Trygis ('of the Vintage') at Propouli in north-west Lemnos\, a chapel of 1706 with a rare icon of the Virgin in white\, is the island's main Dormition pilgrimage: services from the 13th\, liturgy and procession on the morning of the 15th\, vespers at 17:00\, served by monks of Simonopetra. Hundreds come from all over the island\; combine with Myrina's own Koimisis parish feast (14-15 August).\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lemnos/#propouli-feast-of-panagia-tis-trygis-propouli
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lemnos/#propouli-feast-of-panagia-tis-trygis-propouli
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:leros-xirokampos-panigiri-of-panagia-kavouradena-xirokampos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Kavouradena\, Xirokampos
LOCATION:Xirokampos\, Leros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Leros' most photogenic chapel\, wedged between the rocks 800 m along the coast track from Xirokampos beach\, where a fisherman found the icon among crabs (kavouria). It is kept on 15 August with a liturgy and blessing at the chapel and a small feast in Xirokampos afterwards. Walk along the shore from the beach\; there is no parking at the chapel.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/leros/#xirokampos-panigiri-of-panagia-kavouradena-xirokampos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/leros/#xirokampos-panigiri-of-panagia-kavouradena-xirokampos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lesvos-petra-feast-of-panagia-glykofilousa-petra-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Feast of Panagia Glykofilousa\, Petra
LOCATION:Petra\, Lesvos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Petra's landmark church sits on a 40 m rock in the middle of the village\, reached by 114 steps\; on the eve and day of the Dormition it fills with pilgrims and the village below with tavernas and music. Petra also keeps the 'Enniamera' (22-23 August) at the Faneromeni chapel. Combine with the beach and the Molyvos road\; parking in Petra on the 15th is hopeless\, so come early.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#petra-feast-of-panagia-glykofilousa-petra
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#petra-feast-of-panagia-glykofilousa-petra
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lesvos-agiasos-pilgrimage-of-the-dormition-agiasos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Pilgrimage of the Dormition\, Agiasos
LOCATION:Agiasos\, Lesvos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The mountain town of Agiasos and its church of Panagia (Agia Sion) host the great Dormition pilgrimage of the northern Aegean: pilgrims walk the 27 km from Mytilene on the night of 14 August and sleep in the church courtyard\, the icon is carried round the church after the liturgy\, and the square then fills with folk orchestras and dancing. Agiasos is also famous for its own musicians and carnival\, so the party is genuine. Cars are stopped at the edge of town\; go by bus or walk in.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#agiasos-pilgrimage-of-the-dormition-agiasos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#agiasos-pilgrimage-of-the-dormition-agiasos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mykonos-ano-mera-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-tourliani-ano-mera-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri of Panagia Tourliani\, Ano Mera
LOCATION:Ano Mera\, Mykonos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The monastery of Panagia Tourliani in Ano Mera's square is the island's spiritual centre\, and on the evening of 14 August\, after the vespers\, the square fills with a free traditional panigiri: local musicians (Lefteris Kantenas in 2026)\, wine\, and dancing until late\, then the liturgy and procession on the 15th. Ano Mera is 15 minutes by bus from Chora and the buses run late that night.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/mykonos/#ano-mera-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-tourliani-ano-mera
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/mykonos/#ano-mera-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-tourliani-ano-mera
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:naxos-filoti-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-filotitissa-filoti-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270817
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri of Panagia Filotitissa\, Filoti
LOCATION:Filoti\, Naxos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Major panigiri across the inland villages\, especially Filoti — three days of music\, food and dancing. The biggest celebration on the island.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#filoti-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-filotitissa-filoti
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#filoti-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-filotitissa-filoti
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:naxos-apeiranthos-dormition-panigiri-apeiranthos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri\, Apeiranthos
LOCATION:Apeiranthos\, Naxos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Apeiranthos\, the marble-paved village with Cretan roots\, does its own Dormition feast on 14-15 August with the village's celebrated violin players\, kotsakia (improvised rhyming couplets)\, local wine and food in the square\, competing with Filoti a few kilometres away. If you want a slightly smaller crowd and the best musicians\, this is the one.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#apeiranthos-dormition-panigiri-apeiranthos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#apeiranthos-dormition-panigiri-apeiranthos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nisyros-mandraki-panigiri-of-panagia-spiliani-mandraki-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Spiliani\, Mandraki
LOCATION:Mandraki\, Nisyros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Pilgrimage to the cave-monastery above Mandraki. Major island festival\; processions and an all-night panigiri.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/nisyros/#mandraki-panigiri-of-panagia-spiliani-mandraki
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/nisyros/#mandraki-panigiri-of-panagia-spiliani-mandraki
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:paros-parikia-dormition-at-panagia-ekatontapyliani-parikia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition at Panagia Ekatontapyliani\, Parikia
LOCATION:Parikia\, Paros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Procession of the icon from the Church of Ekatontapyliani in Parikia\, one of the oldest standing churches in Greece (4th century). Major all-island festival.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#parikia-dormition-at-panagia-ekatontapyliani-parikia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#parikia-dormition-at-panagia-ekatontapyliani-parikia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:patmos-geranou-north-patmos-panigiri-of-panagia-geranou-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Geranou
LOCATION:Geranou (north Patmos)\, Patmos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The largest panigiri on Patmos\, at the old double chapel on the hilltop of Geranou\, north of Kampos\, with a view over the strait: after the vespers on the 14th thousands crowd the courtyard for food and wine and a traditional orchestra keeps the dancing going until dawn. Go by bus or scooter and expect to walk the last stretch\; cars queue on the narrow road.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/patmos/#geranou-north-patmos-panigiri-of-panagia-geranou
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/patmos/#geranou-north-patmos-panigiri-of-panagia-geranou
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:paxos-gaios-panagia-islet-feast-of-the-dormition-on-panagia-islet--2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Feast of the Dormition on Panagia islet\, Gaios
LOCATION:Gaios (Panagia islet)\, Paxos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 14–15 August the whole of Paxos crosses to the monastery of Panagia Vellianiton on the islet that closes Gaios harbour: vespers and vigil on the eve\, liturgy in the morning\, and then the centuries-old custom of the islanders serving beef broth (zomos) and meat cooked in copper cauldrons to every pilgrim\, local or visitor. Five or six local boatmen shuttle from the Gaios quay from early morning for a small fare\; the wait was minimal in 2026.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paxos/#gaios-panagia-islet-feast-of-the-dormition-on-panagia-islet-
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paxos/#gaios-panagia-islet-feast-of-the-dormition-on-panagia-islet-
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:psara-psara-feast-of-the-dormition-at-the-monastery-psara-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Feast of the Dormition at the monastery\, Psara
LOCATION:Psara\, Psara\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the eve\, 14 August\, islanders and returning Psarians go up to the monastery of the Dormition for vespers\, after which the church serves chickpeas to the fasting pilgrims\; the party then moves to the old threshing floor\, where a small panigiri has been revived in recent years. A rare chance to see the island full\; boats from Chios are booked out that week.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/psara/#psara-feast-of-the-dormition-at-the-monastery-psara
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/psara/#psara-feast-of-the-dormition-at-the-monastery-psara
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pserimos-avlakia-panigiri-of-panagia-avlakia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia\, Avlakia
LOCATION:Avlakia\, Pserimos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Pserimos\, the 30-person islet between Kos and Kalymnos\, has its one big day on 15 August: caiques from Kalymnos and Kos bring hundreds for the liturgy at the Panagia church at Avlakia\, then traditional music\, dancing and local food on the beach front. The excursion boats go back in the afternoon\, so if you want the evening\, arrange a room or a return caique in advance.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/pserimos/#avlakia-panigiri-of-panagia-avlakia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/pserimos/#avlakia-panigiri-of-panagia-avlakia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rhodes-kremasti-panigiri-of-panagia-kremasti-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270823
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia\, Kremasti
LOCATION:Kremasti\, Rhodes\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Dormition feast at the big Panagia church of Kremasti\, near the airport\, turns into a nine-day fair (roughly 14-23 August) with a huge street market\, funfair rides\, food stalls and evening concerts on the square. The religious high point is the vespers and procession on the evening of the 14th. Traffic on the airport road is heavy those nights\; come by bus from Rhodes town or park well outside the village.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rhodes/#kremasti-panigiri-of-panagia-kremasti
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rhodes/#kremasti-panigiri-of-panagia-kremasti
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:santorini-mesa-gonia-episkopi-gonias-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-epi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri of Panagia Episkopi\, Mesa Gonia
LOCATION:Mesa Gonia (Episkopi Gonias)\, Santorini\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The 11th-century Byzantine church of Panagia Episkopi at Mesa Gonia hosts the island's largest panigiri: on the evening of 14 August big cauldrons of fava and beans are cooked in the courtyard\, and after the liturgy on the 15th everyone eats free and dances to live island music with locals and summer visitors mixed together. Park along the Kamari road and walk up\; it gets very busy after 21:00.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/santorini/#mesa-gonia-episkopi-gonias-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-epi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/santorini/#mesa-gonia-episkopi-gonias-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-epi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:schoinoussa-chora-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-akathi-chora-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri of Panagia Akathi\, Chora
LOCATION:Chora\, Schoinoussa\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Panagia Akathi in Chora is the island's church\, and its Dormition feast on 14-15 August is the one night of the year the whole of Schinoussa\, plus visitors from Iraklia and Koufonisi\, sits down together: patatato and other local dishes served free after the liturgy\, wine\, and violin-and-laouto dancing until late. Book a room well ahead\; the island has few.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/schoinoussa/#chora-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-akathi-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/schoinoussa/#chora-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-akathi-chora
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:serifos-ramos-pyrgos-dormition-panigiria-of-serifos-ramos-skopoi-pyr-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270817
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiria of Serifos (Ramos\, Skopoi\, Pyrgos\, Liomantra)
LOCATION:Ramos / Pyrgos\, Serifos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Serifos spreads Dekapentavgoustos over several nights: on the eve (14 Aug) the Panagia chapels at Ramos and Skopoi (Skopiani) and the Evangelistria in Kato Chora celebrate\, on the 15th–16th the feast moves to Pyrgos and Panagia at Liomantra (Sklavogianni)\, and the nine-day (Enniamera) feasts at Kamaroti\, Maskailia and Pente Pigadia run on 20–23 August. Local sources also refer to a three-day 'Xylopanagia' feast at the village of Panagia\; treat that as the 15–16 August cluster. Each is a ktitores' table of fava\, goat and wine with dancing — pick one per night and ask in Livadi which has music.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#ramos-pyrgos-dormition-panigiria-of-serifos-ramos-skopoi-pyr
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#ramos-pyrgos-dormition-panigiria-of-serifos-ramos-skopoi-pyr
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:skyros-skyros-chora-area-panigiri-of-panagia-15-august-megklou-and--2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia (15 August)\, Megklou and Pathima
LOCATION:Skyros Chora area\, Skyros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Skyros keeps Dekapentavgoustos at the chapels of Panagia Megklou (14-15 August) and Panagia Pathima (eve of the 14th)\, with the usual tavles and all-night music\, and on the 15th the island's Skyrian wedding re-enactment in the Chora. It is peak season on a small island with one ferry a day from Kymi\, so accommodation and the boat need booking well ahead.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skyros/#skyros-chora-area-panigiri-of-panagia-15-august-megklou-and-
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skyros/#skyros-chora-area-panigiri-of-panagia-15-august-megklou-and-
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:syros-kini-fotarida-custom-and-dormition-night-kini-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Fotarida custom and Dormition night\, Kini
LOCATION:Kini\, Syros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the evening of 14 August the fishing village of Kini revives the Fotarida\, the old night-fishing lanterns lit along the beach\, followed by an island evening with live music\, and on the 15th the Catholic parish celebrates the Dormition\, as do Galissas\, Pagos\, Piskopio and Chalandriani. Kini's beach tavernas are packed that night\; book.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/syros/#kini-fotarida-custom-and-dormition-night-kini
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/syros/#kini-fotarida-custom-and-dormition-night-kini
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:telendos-telendos-panigiri-of-panagia-telendos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia\, Telendos
LOCATION:Telendos\, Telendos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The car-free islet across the strait from Myrties keeps its own Dormition feast on 15 August\, the quieter alternative to Kalymnos' Kyra Psili: liturgy at the Panagia church\, then food and music in the tavernas along the little waterfront. The Myrties water taxi runs every half hour until late\, so you can hop over for the evening.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/telendos/#telendos-panigiri-of-panagia-telendos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/telendos/#telendos-panigiri-of-panagia-telendos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tinos-tinos-chora-dormition-of-the-virgin-at-panagia-evangelistria-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition of the Virgin at Panagia Evangelistria\, Chora
LOCATION:Tinos Chora\, Tinos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The largest religious pilgrimage in Greece. Pilgrims crawl the kilometre from the port to the Church of Panagia Evangelistria on hands and knees. Book accommodation months in advance.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/tinos/#tinos-chora-dormition-of-the-virgin-at-panagia-evangelistria
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/tinos/#tinos-chora-dormition-of-the-virgin-at-panagia-evangelistria
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:alonnisos-palia-alonnisos-dekapentavgoustos-panigiri-and-alonnisian-we-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dekapentavgoustos panigiri and Alonnisian wedding\, Palia Alonnisos (Chora)
LOCATION:Palia Alonnisos\, Alonnisos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the evening of 15 August the Cultural Association stages a re-enactment of a traditional Alonnisian wedding in the old hilltop village\, in costume with the old songs\, at about 7 pm\, and from 8.30 the municipality's panigiri takes over with violin\, bouzouki and singers until dawn (in 2026 the glenti moved down to the harbour at 9.30 pm). The lanes of the Chora are car-free and the road up is a bottleneck\, so use the bus from Patitiri and walk back down the kalderimi if you are still standing.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/alonnisos/#palia-alonnisos-dekapentavgoustos-panigiri-and-alonnisian-we
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/alonnisos/#palia-alonnisos-dekapentavgoustos-panigiri-and-alonnisian-we
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:andros-panagia-of-panachrantou-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panagia of Panachrantou
LOCATION:Andros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Pilgrimage to the cliff-top monastery above Korthi. The icon is revered for healing properties\; villages across the island send delegations.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/andros/#panagia-of-panachrantou
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/andros/#panagia-of-panachrantou
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:chania-anopoli-graviera-festival-anopoli-sfakion-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Graviera Festival\, Anopoli Sfakion
LOCATION:Anopoli\, Crete (Chania)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the evening of 15 August the Anopoli cultural association and the Municipality of Sfakia lay a communal table on the plateau above Chora Sfakion: boiled meat with pilafi\, Sfakian stew\, graviera\, honey and wine\, with a Cretan kompania and the local dance society. It has run since the mid-1980s and draws people from all over Crete. Start is around 9 pm\; drive up the hairpins from Chora Sfakion in daylight and park on the plateau road.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chania/#anopoli-graviera-festival-anopoli-sfakion
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chania/#anopoli-graviera-festival-anopoli-sfakion
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:evia-north-limni-naftiki-vradia-naval-night-of-dekapentavgoustos-limni-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Naftiki Vradia (Naval Night) of Dekapentavgoustos\, Limni
LOCATION:Limni\, Evia (North)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Limni\, an old shipowners' town\, marks the evening of 15 August with a naval night on the harbour: decorated boats\, Bengal lights and flares over the bay\, and music on the quay. Part of the municipal summer programme\; the waterfront is packed\, so come by 8 pm for a table.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-north/#limni-naftiki-vradia-naval-night-of-dekapentavgoustos-limni
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-north/#limni-naftiki-vradia-naval-night-of-dekapentavgoustos-limni
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:evia-south-stouppaioi-tsakaioi-dekapentavgoustos-panigiria-stouppaioi-a-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dekapentavgoustos panigiria\, Stouppaioi and Tsakaioi (Karystos)
LOCATION:Stouppaioi / Tsakaioi\, Evia (South)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Two of the stone hamlets on the slopes above Karystos\, Stouppaioi and Tsakaioi\, hold their Panagia panigiria on 15 August in the schoolyards\, with violin-and-lute circle dances until dawn and home-cooked local dishes. Narrow roads and no lighting\, so drive up in daylight or share a taxi from Karystos.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-south/#stouppaioi-tsakaioi-dekapentavgoustos-panigiria-stouppaioi-a
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-south/#stouppaioi-tsakaioi-dekapentavgoustos-panigiria-stouppaioi-a
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fournoi-fournoi-panigiri-of-the-dormition-on-the-harbour-fournoi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition on the harbour\, Fournoi
LOCATION:Fournoi\, Fournoi\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The island's biggest night: on 15 August from about 20:00 the cultural association sets tables along the harbour for homemade goat dishes\, mezedes and wine\, with a live traditional orchestra and dancing. Ferries from Ikaria and Samos are full that week\; if you are day-tripping there is no late boat back\, so book a room.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/fournoi/#fournoi-panigiri-of-the-dormition-on-the-harbour-fournoi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/fournoi/#fournoi-panigiri-of-the-dormition-on-the-harbour-fournoi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-akamatra-all-day-panigiri-of-the-dormition-akamatra-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:All-day panigiri of the Dormition\, Akamatra
LOCATION:Akamatra\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Akamatra\, the pretty mountain village above Evdilos\, runs an all-day 15 August panigiri in its central square organised by the association 'I Kefala': violins from 13:00 (two different ensembles in 2026\, Panagiotis Choutras and Nikos Kochylas) through to the following morning. It is the sensible choice if Langada sounds like too much: paved road\, a real square\, food all day. Karavostamo\, Gialiskari\, Kouniadoi\, Monokampi\, Kampa\, Perdiki and Panagia all celebrate the same day.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#akamatra-all-day-panigiri-of-the-dormition-akamatra
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#akamatra-all-day-panigiri-of-the-dormition-akamatra
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-kampa-day-panigiri-of-the-dormition-kampa-xylosyrtis-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Day panigiri of the Dormition\, Kampa (Xylosyrtis)
LOCATION:Kampa\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kampa is the vineyard hamlet above Xylosyrtis under Mount Atheras\; its 15 August panigiri\, run by the Xylosyrtis association 'O Atheras'\, starts early afternoon with local food\, the area's own wine and a violin-led band (Giannis Roussos in 2026) and goes 'until the shoes melt'. A daytime option on the south side of the island\, 15 minutes from Agios Kirykos. Monokampi\, further along the same coast\, also does a midday-start panigiri this date.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#kampa-day-panigiri-of-the-dormition-kampa-xylosyrtis
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#kampa-day-panigiri-of-the-dormition-kampa-xylosyrtis
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-karavostamo-panigiri-of-the-dormition-karavostamo-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition\, Karavostamo
LOCATION:Karavostamo\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The north coast's big 15 August\, held on the day in Karavostamo 'from early' with an Ikarian company (Marios and his group in 2024). Larger and more accessible than Langada\, on the main road between Evdilos and Agios Kirykos\, with the sea a few steps away for a swim between dances. Buses do not run late\; arrange a taxi or a sober driver.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#karavostamo-panigiri-of-the-dormition-karavostamo
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#karavostamo-panigiri-of-the-dormition-karavostamo
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-langada-panigiri-of-the-dormition-langada-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition\, Langada
LOCATION:Langada\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The most famous panigiri in Greece. In the near-abandoned village of Langada above Agios Dimitrios\, the Dormition draws people from across the island and the diaspora for an all-night feast that ends well after sunrise. Communal\, unhurried\, wine-and-dance till dawn — the clearest window into why Ikarians live so long.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#langada-panigiri-of-the-dormition-langada
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#langada-panigiri-of-the-dormition-langada
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-gialiskari-seaside-panigiri-of-the-dormition-gialiskari-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Seaside panigiri of the Dormition\, Gialiskari
LOCATION:Gialiskari\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The fishing hamlet of Gialiskari next to Armenistis\, with its white chapel on the rocks\, celebrates 15 August right by the water\, organised by the cultural association 'I Koimisis': Ikarian wine\, goat and local dishes\, with Stroupa and the Zevkalides playing in 2023\, until morning. Ideal if you are based in Armenistis and do not want the Langada trek\; walk over along the beach.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#gialiskari-seaside-panigiri-of-the-dormition-gialiskari
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#gialiskari-seaside-panigiri-of-the-dormition-gialiskari
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ithaca-platrithias-panigiri-of-the-dormition-platrithias-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition\, Platrithias
LOCATION:Platrithias\, Ithaca\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The island's central 15 August liturgy is in Platrithias\, and the evening panigiri in its big square marks the unofficial end of the Ithacan summer: live band\, barbecues\, pop-up bars and dancing until dawn\, with the whole island and every returned emigrant there. Rooms in the north are full that week\; plan to sleep in Vathy and drive.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ithaca/#platrithias-panigiri-of-the-dormition-platrithias
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ithaca/#platrithias-panigiri-of-the-dormition-platrithias
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kea-ioulida-tziotiko-panigiri-of-the-dormition-ioulida-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Tziotiko panigiri of the Dormition\, Ioulida
LOCATION:Ioulida\, Kea (Tzia)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kea's big night: on 15 August from 21:00 the municipality throws the 'Traditional Tziotiko Panigiri' in the main square of Ioulida\, with a full island orchestra\, communal tables and dancing that goes on until the small hours. The next evening (16 Aug\, 20:00) the party moves to Kato Meria for the 'Glenti Kato Merias' organised with the Karthaia society. Ioulida is on foot only — expect a long walk from wherever you find parking.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kea/#ioulida-tziotiko-panigiri-of-the-dormition-ioulida
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kea/#ioulida-tziotiko-panigiri-of-the-dormition-ioulida
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kefalonia-omala-agios-gerasimos-monastery-feast-of-agios-gerasimos-oma-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270817
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Gerasimos\, Omala monastery
LOCATION:Omala (Agios Gerasimos monastery)\, Kefalonia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Patron saint of Kefalonia. Major pilgrimage to the monastery in Omala valley\; the saint's relics are paraded. The 16/8 procession is the larger of the two annual events.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kefalonia/#omala-agios-gerasimos-monastery-feast-of-agios-gerasimos-oma
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kefalonia/#omala-agios-gerasimos-monastery-feast-of-agios-gerasimos-oma
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kefalonia-komitata-panigiri-of-komitata-erisos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270817
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Komitata\, Erisos
LOCATION:Komitata\, Kefalonia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The northern village of Komitata\, on the Erisos peninsula between Agia Efimia and Fiskardo\, holds a two-day panigiri on 15–16 August run by the village cultural association: church in the morning\, then long tables\, grilled meat\, wine and a live orchestra in the square both nights. Pyrgi on the Sami side has its own on the 16th and Antipata/Pylaros on the 14th if you are touring.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kefalonia/#komitata-panigiri-of-komitata-erisos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kefalonia/#komitata-panigiri-of-komitata-erisos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:koufonisia-kato-koufonisi-dormition-panigiri-on-kato-koufonisi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri on Kato Koufonisi
LOCATION:Kato Koufonisi\, Koufonisia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 15 August the whole island crosses by caique to the uninhabited Kato Koufonisi for the liturgy at the church of the Virgin\, followed by a free meal of fish and meat in the courtyard and a panigiri with kerasmata and violins\; the return crossing is an informal race between the boats\, and the winner's crew is feasted again. Boats fill up\, so be at the harbour early in the morning.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/koufonisia/#kato-koufonisi-dormition-panigiri-on-kato-koufonisi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/koufonisia/#kato-koufonisi-dormition-panigiri-on-kato-koufonisi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kythira-potamos-panigiri-of-the-dormition-potamos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition\, Potamos
LOCATION:Potamos\, Kythira\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Potamos\, the market town of the north\, throws its annual chorós on the night of 15 August in the big square\, organised by the Potamos cultural association: live orchestra\, tables\, grilled meat and wine\, and the whole north of the island plus the returned Australians dancing until late. The square is small for the crowd\; eat first at one of the tavernas around it and drift in around 11pm.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythira/#potamos-panigiri-of-the-dormition-potamos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythira/#potamos-panigiri-of-the-dormition-potamos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lasithi-armeni-panigiri-of-the-dormition-armeni-sitia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition\, Armeni (Sitia)
LOCATION:Armeni\, Crete (Lasithi)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Armeni\, a few kilometres inland from Sitia\, holds the area's best-attended Dormition glenti on the night of 15 August in the schoolyard\, with a full menu (15 euros in 2025) and a name kompania (Giorgos and Nikos Stratakis in 2025)\; Paraspori nearby does its Panagia the night before. Reserve through the village association and expect it to run until 3 am.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lasithi/#armeni-panigiri-of-the-dormition-armeni-sitia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lasithi/#armeni-panigiri-of-the-dormition-armeni-sitia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:milos-zefyria-dormition-feast-at-panagia-portiani-zefyria-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270817
SUMMARY:Dormition feast at Panagia Portiani\, Zefyria
LOCATION:Zefyria\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Zefyria\, the island's old capital\, celebrates the Dormition at Panagia Portiani with vespers and bread-blessing at 20:00 on 14 August\, liturgy at 07:30 on the 15th and the glenti itself on the evening of 15 August\, with a band (violin\, bouzouki\, keyboards\, laouto\, vocals) and refreshments in the churchyard. Because the party is on the 15th rather than the eve\, you can do Adamas on the 14th–15th and Zefyria the same night — the two are ten minutes apart by car.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#zefyria-dormition-feast-at-panagia-portiani-zefyria
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#zefyria-dormition-feast-at-panagia-portiani-zefyria
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:milos-adamas-dormition-panigiri-adamas-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270817
SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri\, Adamas
LOCATION:Adamas\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The port's Dekapentavgoustos: vespers and bread-blessing at 20:00 on 14 August followed by a procession of the icon around the harbour\, liturgy at 07:30 on the 15th\, and from 21:30 on the 15th a traditional glenti with violins and laouto in the church courtyard. It is the busiest night of the year in Adamas — book dinner and accommodation well ahead\, and expect the harbour road to be closed for the procession.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#adamas-dormition-panigiri-adamas
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#adamas-dormition-panigiri-adamas
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:othonoi-othonoi-panigiri-of-the-dormition-othonoi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition\, Othonoi
LOCATION:Othonoi\, Othonoi\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:15 August is the one night of the year Othonoi is full: emigrants back from America and Corfu\, liturgy in the morning\, and a panigiri with music and food by the harbour that goes late. Rooms are few\, so book months ahead or come on the day-boat from Agios Stefanos and go back on the late run.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/othonoi/#othonoi-panigiri-of-the-dormition-othonoi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/othonoi/#othonoi-panigiri-of-the-dormition-othonoi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rethymno-atsipopoulo-panigiri-of-the-dormition-atsipopoulo-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition\, Atsipopoulo
LOCATION:Atsipopoulo\, Crete (Rethymno)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The large village on the hill just west of Rethymno throws the town's nearest big Dormition glenti on the night of 15 August\, with a headline Cretan singer (Manolis Kontaros in 2019\, Grigoris Samolis for the Asteras club's anniversary in 2025) and tables that are reserved by phone in advance. It is five minutes from the city\, so taxis are easy\; expect it to run past 3 am.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rethymno/#atsipopoulo-panigiri-of-the-dormition-atsipopoulo
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rethymno/#atsipopoulo-panigiri-of-the-dormition-atsipopoulo
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rethymno-lampini-panigiri-of-the-dormition-lampini-agios-vasileios-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition\, Lampini (Agios Vasileios)
LOCATION:Lampini\, Crete (Rethymno)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Lampini's Byzantine church of the Panagia\, with its frescoes\, is the reason the whole Agios Vasileios valley comes here on 15 August: liturgy in the morning and a glenti in the evening with a well-known lyra player (Andreas Manolarakis in 2019\, Nikos Manioudakis in 2025). Twenty minutes south of Rethymno on the Spili road\, easy to combine with the Preveli coast.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rethymno/#lampini-panigiri-of-the-dormition-lampini-agios-vasileios
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rethymno/#lampini-panigiri-of-the-dormition-lampini-agios-vasileios
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:samothrace-chora-panigiri-of-the-dormition-chora-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Dormition\, Chora
LOCATION:Chora\, Samothrace\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The island capital's big night: on the evening of 15 August the square of Chora\, under the castle\, hosts a traditional panigiri with local musicians and dancing. Chora keeps the Transfiguration (6 August) the same way. Both are busy with the August camping crowd from Therma\, so come up early for a seat.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samothrace/#chora-panigiri-of-the-dormition-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samothrace/#chora-panigiri-of-the-dormition-chora
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sikinos-panagia-pantanassa-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panagia Pantanassa
LOCATION:Sikinos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The big island festival at the church above Chora. Music until dawn — entirely local\, almost no tourists.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sikinos/#panagia-pantanassa
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sikinos/#panagia-pantanassa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:skopelos-glossa-loutraki-panigiri-of-panagia-15-august-glossa-and-lou-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270816
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia (15 August)\, Glossa and Loutraki
LOCATION:Glossa / Loutraki\, Skopelos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The north of the island celebrates Dekapentavgoustos twice over: the municipality's panigiri on the little harbour of Loutraki (15 August in 2025\, the 16th in 2026\, with a local singer and dancing by the water)\, and since 2025 a revived all-night glenti in the central square of Glossa village above it\, where the music went on until 6 am. Between them there is a shuttle-worthy 3 km of hairpins\, so decide where you will sleep\; rooms in Glossa are few and go early in August.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skopelos/#glossa-loutraki-panigiri-of-panagia-15-august-glossa-and-lou
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skopelos/#glossa-loutraki-panigiri-of-panagia-15-august-glossa-and-lou
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:corfu-kato-garouna-three-day-panigiri-of-kato-garouna-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270819
SUMMARY:Three-day panigiri of Kato Garouna
LOCATION:Kato Garouna\, Corfu\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kato Garouna\, above Agios Gordios on the west coast\, is famous on Corfu for its musicians ('Ta paidia ap' to Garouna') and throws a three-day panigiri from 16 August with its own players\, long tables of pastitsada and sofrito and dancing every night\; the village also does a wine festival on a Saturday at the very end of August. Twenty minutes from town\; go on the first night\, which is the most local.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#kato-garouna-three-day-panigiri-of-kato-garouna
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#kato-garouna-three-day-panigiri-of-kato-garouna
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:evia-south-marmari-harbour-panigiri-of-16-august-marmari-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270817
SUMMARY:Harbour panigiri of 16 August\, Marmari
LOCATION:Marmari\, Evia (South)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The ferry port of Marmari\, an hour from Rafina\, follows the Dekapentavgoustos with its own harbour panigiri on the night of 16 August\, with a nisiotika orchestra and singers (Matthaios Giannoulis and Maria Nomikou in 2025) and dancing on the quay. Easy to reach from Athens for a night\; the last boat back is around midnight in summer\, so plan to stay.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-south/#marmari-harbour-panigiri-of-16-august-marmari
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/evia-south/#marmari-harbour-panigiri-of-16-august-marmari
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kythira-pitsinianika-panigiri-of-pitsinianika-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270817
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Pitsinianika
LOCATION:Pitsinianika\, Kythira\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The day after the Dormition the hamlet of Pitsinianika\, between Livadi and Mylopotamos\, fills its little square from 9pm with traditional\, folk and even jazz music\, food and drink\, a raffle\, and the Kythiran circle dance 'apanochoro' danced by everyone. Run by the village association\, 3 euro entry\, one of the friendliest nights on the island.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythira/#pitsinianika-panigiri-of-pitsinianika
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythira/#pitsinianika-panigiri-of-pitsinianika
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lasithi-piskokefalo-sultanina-raisin-festival-piskokefalo-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270817
SUMMARY:Sultanina (raisin) Festival\, Piskokefalo
LOCATION:Piskokefalo\, Crete (Lasithi)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Sitia's raisin festival is held in Piskokefalo\, the sultana village 4 km south of town\, at the athletic centre on the evening of 16 August\, with raisin-based sweets and dishes\, local wine and a big Cretan stage (Grigoris Samolis in 2025). It closes the Kornaria panigiri weekend\, so it is the one to pick if you can only do one Sitia glenti\; Piskokefalo also holds a corn festival there on 19 July.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lasithi/#piskokefalo-sultanina-raisin-festival-piskokefalo
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lasithi/#piskokefalo-sultanina-raisin-festival-piskokefalo
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rethymno-eleftherna-august-panigiri-of-eleftherna-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270817
SUMMARY:August panigiri of Eleftherna
LOCATION:Eleftherna\, Crete (Rethymno)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The day after the Dormition the Eleftherna cultural association holds its glenti at the Panorama centre opposite the archaeological museum\, with two Cretan singers on stage (Tzanidakis and Samolis in 2019). It is a good way to pair a museum visit with an evening of music\; the site is 30 minutes from Rethymno past Arkadi.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rethymno/#eleftherna-august-panigiri-of-eleftherna
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rethymno/#eleftherna-august-panigiri-of-eleftherna
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ios-mersinia-panigiri-of-panagia-at-mersinia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270820
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270822
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia at Mersinia
LOCATION:Mersinia\, Ios\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The chapel of the Virgin at Mersinia\, in the countryside north of Chora\, holds its own feast on 21 August with a vespers the evening before\, food and wine offered by the families who look after the church\, and music. A small rural panigiri\; ask in Chora for directions and a lift.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ios/#mersinia-panigiri-of-panagia-at-mersinia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ios/#mersinia-panigiri-of-panagia-at-mersinia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:folegandros-karavostasi-kaikokakavia-fish-soup-festival-karavostasi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270821
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270822
SUMMARY:Kaikokakavia fish-soup festival\, Karavostasi
LOCATION:Karavostasi\, Folegandros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:A harbour evening in Karavostasi built around kakavia\, the fishermen's soup: the local boats' catch is cooked in big pots on the quay and served free with wine\, with island music afterwards. Held on 21 August\; arrive early with a plate and a spoon of your own if you can\, and eat standing — there are few tables.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/folegandros/#karavostasi-kaikokakavia-fish-soup-festival-karavostasi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/folegandros/#karavostasi-kaikokakavia-fish-soup-festival-karavostasi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:arki-arki-panigiri-of-panagia-nine-day-arki-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia (nine-day)\, Arki
LOCATION:Arki\, Arki\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Arki\, with its 40-odd inhabitants\, has one feast a year worth crossing for: the ninth day of the Dormition on 23 August\, when boats from Patmos and Lipsi bring people for the vespers at the Panagia church and a feast of fish and goat by the sea\, with music and dancing by the harbour. Get there and back on a caique from Patmos or Lipsi the same day\, or stay in one of the few rooms.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/arki/#arki-panigiri-of-panagia-nine-day-arki
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/arki/#arki-panigiri-of-panagia-nine-day-arki
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:corfu-gastouri-panigiri-of-panagia-odigitria-gastouri-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Odigitria\, Gastouri
LOCATION:Gastouri\, Corfu\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Odigitria on 23 August (the leave-taking of the Dormition) is a second 15 August for a string of Corfu villages: Gastouri\, below the Achilleion\, holds vespers on the 22nd and a panigiri in the square with an orchestra and food\, and Pelekas\, Agioi Deka\, Liapades and Pentati do the same. Good option if you missed the mid-August crowds.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#gastouri-panigiri-of-panagia-odigitria-gastouri
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/corfu/#gastouri-panigiri-of-panagia-odigitria-gastouri
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kythnos-flabouria-nine-day-feast-of-panagia-flabouriani-flabouria-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Nine-day feast of Panagia Flabouriani\, Flabouria
LOCATION:Flabouria\, Kythnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Named by the municipality among the island's most important feasts: the nine-day of the Dormition at Panagia Flabouriani\, the chapel by the west-coast beach of Flabouria\, on the evening of 22 August and the morning of the 23rd\, with the usual violin-laouto glenti. Panagia Eleousa at Kastro celebrates the same date. The last stretch to Flabouria is a rough track from Chora — a 4x4 or a walk.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#flabouria-nine-day-feast-of-panagia-flabouriani-flabouria
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#flabouria-nine-day-feast-of-panagia-flabouriani-flabouria
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lasithi-sykia-fig-festival-sykia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270823
SUMMARY:Fig Festival\, Sykia
LOCATION:Sykia\, Crete (Lasithi)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:A young festival (4th edition in 2025) in the hill village of Sykia west of Sitia\, on the evening of 22 August: fresh and dried figs\, fig sweets and raki\, with local lyra players (Fasoulas and Kallergis in 2025) and a 5-euro entry. Small and friendly\; go for the food rather than a big stage.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lasithi/#sykia-fig-festival-sykia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lasithi/#sykia-fig-festival-sykia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:leipsoi-lipsi-village-panigiri-of-panagia-tou-charou-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270825
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia tou Charou
LOCATION:Lipsi village\, Leipsoi\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The feast Leipsoi is known for\, on the ninth day of the Dormition: the icon of Panagia tou Charou (the Virgin holding the crucified Christ) is famous for the dried lilies placed on it on 25 March that bud again in August. On 22 August at 6 pm the icon is carried in procession from the cathedral with the band and the whole island\, and the municipality hands out grapes\, sweets\, mastic-and-anise bread and local meat over three days of music. Boats come from Patmos\, Leros and Kos\; book the ferry back before you go.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/leipsoi/#lipsi-village-panigiri-of-panagia-tou-charou
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/leipsoi/#lipsi-village-panigiri-of-panagia-tou-charou
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lemnos-kotsinas-enniamera-of-the-virgin-at-zoodochos-pigi-kotsinas-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Enniamera of the Virgin at Zoodochos Pigi\, Kotsinas
LOCATION:Kotsinas\, Lemnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The historic chapel of Zoodochos Pigi at Kotsinas\, by the statue of Maroula on Bournia bay\, keeps the ninth day after the Dormition with festive vespers at 19:30 on 22 August and liturgy at 07:30 on the 23rd. A quiet\, scenic feast rather than a party\; the underground spring beneath the church is the reason people come.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lemnos/#kotsinas-enniamera-of-the-virgin-at-zoodochos-pigi-kotsinas
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lemnos/#kotsinas-enniamera-of-the-virgin-at-zoodochos-pigi-kotsinas
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lesvos-agia-paraskevi-panigiri-of-panagia-mosna-with-donkey-races-a-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Mosna with donkey races\, Agia Paraskevi
LOCATION:Agia Paraskevi\, Lesvos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The folklore society of Agia Paraskevi has run this two-day feast since 1985 at the chapel of Panagia Mosna\, 2.5 km above the village: on 22 August a garlanded calf is led through the village at midday\, society members ride decorated donkeys up to the chapel in the evening and the music goes all night\; on the 23rd there is liturgy\, blessed 'kiskek' (wheat and meat stew cooked overnight) for everyone\, donkey races at Ligaridia in the afternoon and dancing in the village square till dawn. The rural end of the summer for Lesvos\; book a table in the square.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#agia-paraskevi-panigiri-of-panagia-mosna-with-donkey-races-a
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#agia-paraskevi-panigiri-of-panagia-mosna-with-donkey-races-a
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:milos-komia-panigiri-of-panagia-giatrissa-komia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Giatrissa\, Komia
LOCATION:Komia\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Komia celebrates the nine-day (Enniamera) of the Panagia at the chapel of Panagia Giatrissa — 'the Healer' — with vespers and a panigiri in the churchyard on the evening of 22 August. It is one of the island's older rural feasts and draws Milians from every village\; the same evening the Panagia chapels at Kipos and Trypiti also celebrate\, so ask locals which one has the band that year.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#komia-panigiri-of-panagia-giatrissa-komia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#komia-panigiri-of-panagia-giatrissa-komia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mykonos-xlsior-mykonos-lgbtq-festival-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270831
SUMMARY:XLSIOR Mykonos (LGBTQ+ festival)
LOCATION:Mykonos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Major international LGBTQ+ summer festival drawing 30\,000+ visitors. Pool parties\, beach events\, headline DJs at Cavo Paradiso and other venues. Mykonos has been a leading gay summer destination since the 1970s\; XLSIOR is the most concentrated week of it. Expect rooms to be impossible.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/mykonos/#xlsior-mykonos-lgbtq-festival
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/mykonos/#xlsior-mykonos-lgbtq-festival
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:naxos-tripodes-vivlos-enniamera-of-the-virgin-tripodes-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Enniamera of the Virgin\, Tripodes
LOCATION:Tripodes (Vivlos)\, Naxos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Nine days after the Dormition\, Tripodes (Vivlos)\, the windmill village above Plaka beach\, holds the Enniamera feast with tables in the square\, wine and live island music. It is the closest big village panigiri to the west-coast beaches and a good one if you are staying around Agios Prokopios or Plaka.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#tripodes-vivlos-enniamera-of-the-virgin-tripodes
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#tripodes-vivlos-enniamera-of-the-virgin-tripodes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nisyros-panagia-kyra-monastery-panigiri-of-panagia-kyra-nine-day-man-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Kyra (nine-day)\, Mandraki
LOCATION:Panagia Kyra monastery\, Nisyros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The 'ninth day' of the Dormition on 22-23 August is kept at the monastery of Panagia Kyra\, in the countryside between Mandraki and Loutra: after vespers huge tables are laid in the monastery courtyard for everyone\, with music until late. Quieter than Spiliani and more of a locals' feast.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/nisyros/#panagia-kyra-monastery-panigiri-of-panagia-kyra-nine-day-man
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/nisyros/#panagia-kyra-monastery-panigiri-of-panagia-kyra-nine-day-man
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:salamis-faneromeni-panigiri-of-panagia-faneromeni-faneromeni-monaste-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Faneromeni\, Faneromeni Monastery
LOCATION:Faneromeni\, Salamina\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The biggest event on Salamina: the 16th-century monastery of Faneromeni on the north-west coast\, opposite Megara\, keeps the Apodosis of the Dormition on 23 August with a vigil on the 22nd\, a procession of the miraculous icon and tens of thousands of pilgrims\, many of whom walk through the night from Paloukia\; a fair with stalls and food lines the road to the monastery. Extra buses run from Paloukia and the Perama ferry\; go on the eve for the atmosphere.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/salamis/#faneromeni-panigiri-of-panagia-faneromeni-faneromeni-monaste
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/salamis/#faneromeni-panigiri-of-panagia-faneromeni-faneromeni-monaste
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tilos-mikro-chorio-panigiri-of-panagia-kamariani-mikro-chorio-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Kamariani\, Mikro Chorio
LOCATION:Mikro Chorio\, Tilos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The ghost village of Mikro Chorio\, abandoned in the 1960s\, fills again on 23 August for the feast of Panagia Kamariani\, with music\, dance and free food among the ruins. Same night as Politissa in Livadia\, ten minutes away\, so pick one.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/tilos/#mikro-chorio-panigiri-of-panagia-kamariani-mikro-chorio
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/tilos/#mikro-chorio-panigiri-of-panagia-kamariani-mikro-chorio
END:VEVENT
