UID:tilos-livadia-panigiri-of-panagia-politissa-livadia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Politissa\, Livadia
LOCATION:Livadia\, Tilos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the ninth day of the Dormition\, 23 August\, the chapel of Panagia Politissa above Livadia bay holds its feast with traditional music\, dancing and free food for everyone. Walk up from the harbour in the evening.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/tilos/#livadia-panigiri-of-panagia-politissa-livadia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/tilos/#livadia-panigiri-of-panagia-politissa-livadia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aegina-aegina-town-feast-of-agios-dionysios-relics-aegina-hospital-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270823
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270825
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Dionysios (relics)\, Aegina Hospital
LOCATION:Aegina Town\, Aegina\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Aegina's hospital is dedicated to Agios Dionysios of Zakynthos\, who was bishop of Aegina and lived on the island\, and the translation of his relics is kept on 23-24 August with an episcopal vespers at 7.30 pm and liturgy and memorial next morning. A town event for those already on the island in late August.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/aegina/#aegina-town-feast-of-agios-dionysios-relics-aegina-hospital
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/aegina/#aegina-town-feast-of-agios-dionysios-relics-aegina-hospital
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:andros-menites-panigiri-of-koumoulo-menites-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270823
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Koumoulo\, Menites
LOCATION:Menites\, Andros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Menites\, the village of running water and plane trees above Chora\, holds its Koumoulo panigiri on 23 August from 21:00 in the square\, run by the cultural association with free entry: local food\, wine and live island music. Katakoilos has its own big square panigiri on a nearby night (22-24 August)\, so you can do both in a weekend.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/andros/#menites-panigiri-of-koumoulo-menites
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/andros/#menites-panigiri-of-koumoulo-menites
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:chios-nea-potamia-nine-days-of-the-virgin-panigiri-nea-potamia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270823
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Nine-days-of-the-Virgin panigiri\, Nea Potamia
LOCATION:Nea Potamia\, Chios\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The 'Enniamera' (ninth day after the Dormition\, 23 August) is kept as a village panigiri in the square of Nea Potamia in north-eastern Chios\, organised by the local association with a traditional orchestra (Poupaloi-Pipidis in 2024). A quieter alternative to the mid-August crowds\, popular with families from Chios town.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chios/#nea-potamia-nine-days-of-the-virgin-panigiri-nea-potamia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chios/#nea-potamia-nine-days-of-the-virgin-panigiri-nea-potamia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mykonos-ano-mera-enniamera-of-the-virgin-ano-mera-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270823
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Enniamera of the Virgin\, Ano Mera
LOCATION:Ano Mera\, Mykonos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Nine days after the Dormition\, Panagia Tourliani in Ano Mera has a second\, quieter panigiri in the monastery square with the local group Aposperites playing island music\, food and wine. Less crowded than the 15th and easier to get a table at the tavernas around the square.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/mykonos/#ano-mera-enniamera-of-the-virgin-ano-mera
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/mykonos/#ano-mera-enniamera-of-the-virgin-ano-mera
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:paros-naoussa-enniamera-and-the-corsair-night-pirate-raid-re-enact-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270823
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270824
SUMMARY:Enniamera and the Corsair Night (pirate raid re-enactment)\, Naoussa
LOCATION:Naoussa\, Paros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 23 August\, the ninth day after the Dormition\, Naoussa's Women's Association ends its Enniamera bazaar and the village youth stage the Koursariko: around 21:00 boats with torches sweep into the old harbour\, 'pirates' dressed as Barbarossa's men (who sacked Naoussa in 1537) snatch the girls\, the locals fight back\, and it all dissolves into a panigiri with violins\, dancing and wine on the quay. Revived in the 1960s and held every year since. Get to the harbour by 20:00 for a spot by the water.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#naoussa-enniamera-and-the-corsair-night-pirate-raid-re-enact
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#naoussa-enniamera-and-the-corsair-night-pirate-raid-re-enact
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:symi-nimos-islet-panigiri-of-panagia-nimos-islet-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270823
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270825
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia\, Nimos islet
LOCATION:Nimos islet\, Symi\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 23-24 August the caiques go north from Gialos to the uninhabited islet of Nimos for the feast of the Panagia (Ypakoi/Alithini chapels) with fish\, wine and music on the shore. Boats are the only way\; ask at the Gialos harbour on the 23rd.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/symi/#nimos-islet-panigiri-of-panagia-nimos-islet
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/symi/#nimos-islet-panigiri-of-panagia-nimos-islet
END:VEVENT
