BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:heraklion-heraklion-feast-of-agios-titos-patron-of-heraklion-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270824
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270826
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Titos\, patron of Heraklion
LOCATION:Heraklion\, Crete (Heraklion)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Heraklion's patron\, the apostle Titus\, is honoured at his basilica off 25 August Street: hierarchical vespers on the 24th\, liturgy and the procession of the saint's skull through the city centre on the 25th\, with the municipal band and the honour guard. It is a city religious event rather than a village glenti\; the street is pedestrian\, and the procession leaves the church mid-morning.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#heraklion-feast-of-agios-titos-patron-of-heraklion
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#heraklion-feast-of-agios-titos-patron-of-heraklion
