UID:andros-ormos-korthiou-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-ormos-korthiou-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270826
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270828
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Fanourios\, Ormos Korthiou
LOCATION:Ormos Korthiou\, Andros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The seaside chapel of Agios Fanourios at Ormos Korthiou celebrates on 26-27 August with vespers\, fanouropita for everyone and an evening glenti on the waterfront. A relaxed late-August feast in the south of the island.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/andros/#ormos-korthiou-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-ormos-korthiou
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/andros/#ormos-korthiou-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-ormos-korthiou
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lemnos-lychna-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-lychna-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270826
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270828
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Fanourios\, Lychna
LOCATION:Lychna\, Lemnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the eve of Agios Fanourios (26 August) the cultural association of Lychna\, near Moudros\, fills the central square from 21:30 with a five-piece Lemnian band\, plenty of food and drink and dancing\, with the municipality as sponsor. Reservations by phone. The last big village night before the September Agios Sozon feast.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lemnos/#lychna-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-lychna
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lemnos/#lychna-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-lychna
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:milos-plaka-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-plaka-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270826
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270828
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Fanourios\, Plaka
LOCATION:Plaka\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Agios Fanourios is celebrated at Plaka\, Pollonia and Trypiti\, but the party is in Plaka: after vespers on the evening of 26 August a panigiri with a DJ and a food canteen takes over the church forecourt. Fanouropites (the saint's oil-and-cinnamon cakes) are blessed and handed round. Plaka is car-free — park at the lots below the village and walk up.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#plaka-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-plaka
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#plaka-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-plaka
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mykonos-mykonos-chora-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-chora-and-ano-mera-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270826
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270828
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Fanourios\, Chora and Ano Mera
LOCATION:Mykonos Chora\, Mykonos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the evening of 26 August the chapels of Agios Fanourios in Chora and at Ano Mera (and the rural one at Chondros Gkremos) hold vespers with fanouropita for everyone\, followed by wine and music. A small\, local end-of-August feast worth catching between the beach clubs.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/mykonos/#mykonos-chora-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-chora-and-ano-mera
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/mykonos/#mykonos-chora-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-chora-and-ano-mera
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:paros-ampelas-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-ampelas-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270826
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270828
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Fanourios\, Ampelas
LOCATION:Ampelas\, Paros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The fishing hamlet of Ampelas\, east of Naoussa\, keeps the feast of Agios Fanourios with vespers at the chapel on the evening of 26 August and a small panigiri with fanouropita\, meze and island music by the water. It is a local\, low-key evening\; combine it with dinner at one of the fish tavernas on the beach.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#ampelas-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-ampelas
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#ampelas-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-ampelas
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rhodes-rhodes-town-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-rhodes-old-town-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270826
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270829
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Fanourios\, Rhodes Old Town
LOCATION:Rhodes Town\, Rhodes\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Agios Fanourios\, the finder of lost things\, has his little 13th-century church in the heart of the Old Town\, and on 25-27 August the lanes around it fill with fanouropites (the spiced cake baked as a vow)\, stalls and evening music. Paradisi holds a separate Agios Fanourios feast on the 26th. Stroll in after 8 pm\; no car needed.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rhodes/#rhodes-town-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-rhodes-old-town
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rhodes/#rhodes-town-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-rhodes-old-town
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:skiathos-skiathos-town-feast-of-agios-fanourios-fanouropita-skiathos--2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270826
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270828
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Fanourios (fanouropita)\, Skiathos Town
LOCATION:Skiathos Town\, Skiathos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The chapel of Agios Fanourios belongs to the parish of Genniseos tis Theotokou in the Chora\; on the evening of 26 August women bring their fanouropites (the spiced saint's cakes) to be blessed from 6 pm\, followed by festive vespers at 8 pm and the liturgy and kollyva next morning. Cakes are cut and shared with everyone present\, so turn up hungry but do not expect music or dancing.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skiathos/#skiathos-town-feast-of-agios-fanourios-fanouropita-skiathos-
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skiathos/#skiathos-town-feast-of-agios-fanourios-fanouropita-skiathos-
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-agios-panteleimonas-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-agios-pantel-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270828
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Fanourios\, Agios Panteleimonas courtyard
LOCATION:Agios Panteleimonas\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Agios Fanourios on 27 August is the last big saint's night of the Ikarian summer\, and it is kept in several places at once: in the church courtyard at Agios Panteleimonas above Agios Kirykos (Zelepos orchestra)\, at Maratho above Evdilos\, at Vrakades and at Agios Dimitrios in Raches. Fanouropita (the saint's cake) is handed round with the goat. By now the August crowds are thinning\, so it feels more local.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#agios-panteleimonas-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-agios-pantel
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#agios-panteleimonas-panigiri-of-agios-fanourios-agios-pantel
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:amorgos-vroutsi-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-vroutsi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis\, Vroutsi
LOCATION:Vroutsi\, Amorgos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The village of Vroutsi in Kato Meria keeps the Beheading of St John with a panigiri on the evening of 28 August: goat patatato\, wine and violins in the small square. A gentle end-of-August feast in the least visited part of the island.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#vroutsi-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-vroutsi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/amorgos/#vroutsi-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-vroutsi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:andros-makrotantalo-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-makrotantal-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Prodromos\, Makrotantalo and Vourkoti
LOCATION:Makrotantalo\, Andros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:For the Beheading of St John on 29 August\, Makrotantalo in the far north keeps the feast with kerasmata and dancing after church\, and the mountain village of Vourkoti above Apoikia holds its big panigiri the same night\, with food\, wine and violins in the square. Vourkoti is the more spectacular setting\; the road up is narrow and unlit.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/andros/#makrotantalo-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-makrotantal
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/andros/#makrotantalo-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-makrotantal
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:astypalaia-agios-ioannis-monastery-west-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodr-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Prodromos (monastery)
LOCATION:Agios Ioannis monastery (west)\, Astypalaia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 28-29 August the panigiri moves to the remote monastery of Agios Ioannis on the wild west of the island\, above the waterfall gorge: vespers\, then food and violins in the courtyard. The last 3 km are dirt track\; go in a group and share a car.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/astypalaia/#agios-ioannis-monastery-west-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodr
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/astypalaia/#agios-ioannis-monastery-west-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodr
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:folegandros-ano-meria-agrosourotoxynotyri-cheese-festival-ano-meria-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270829
SUMMARY:Agrosourotoxynotyri cheese festival\, Ano Meria
LOCATION:Ano Meria\, Folegandros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:A celebration of Folegandros's own sour cheese\, souroto\, and its farm food\, held in Ano Meria on 28 August: cheese\, matsata pasta and local wine offered by the village\, with violin and laouto and dancing until late. It marks the tail end of the season\, when the crowds have thinned and it's mostly Folegandrians in the circle.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/folegandros/#ano-meria-agrosourotoxynotyri-cheese-festival-ano-meria
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/folegandros/#ano-meria-agrosourotoxynotyri-cheese-festival-ano-meria
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:halki-agios-ioannis-alarga-monastery-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-ala-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Alarga
LOCATION:Agios Ioannis Alarga monastery\, Halki\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The monastery of Agios Ioannis 'Alarga' (far away) sits at the end of the road across the island from Nimborio\, and on 28-29 August the whole of Halki plus its Rhodes and Florida diaspora drives\, walks or rides out for the vespers\, a traditional feast in the monastery courtyard and lyra-and-laouto music until late\, then a procession back in the harbour. The municipality runs a shuttle\; go on the 28th evening.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/halki/#agios-ioannis-alarga-monastery-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-ala
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/halki/#agios-ioannis-alarga-monastery-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-ala
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ios-kalamos-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-psathi-and-kalamos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis\, Psathi and Kalamos
LOCATION:Kalamos\, Ios\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:For the Beheading of St John\, two chapels on the wild east coast\, at Psathi bay and above Kalamos beach\, hold their feasts on the same night of 28-29 August: meat soup and fasolada are ladled out free\, with wine and traditional music by the sea. Both are at the end of long dirt roads\; go with a car and a torch\, and stay for the dawn liturgy if you can.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ios/#kalamos-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-psathi-and-kalamos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ios/#kalamos-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-psathi-and-kalamos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:iraklia-cave-of-agios-ioannis-south-of-panagia-vespers-of-agios-ioan-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Vespers of Agios Ioannis in the cave
LOCATION:Cave of Agios Ioannis\, south of Panagia\, Iraklia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the evening of 28 August the vespers for the Beheading of St John is sung inside the first great chamber of the Agios Ioannis cave\, an hour's rough walk south of Panagia\, with candles and crowds who come over from the neighbouring islands\, followed by kerasmata outside. Take a torch and good shoes\; the path is stony and the walk back is in the dark.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/iraklia/#cave-of-agios-ioannis-south-of-panagia-vespers-of-agios-ioan
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/iraklia/#cave-of-agios-ioannis-south-of-panagia-vespers-of-agios-ioan
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:karpathos-olympos-vrykounta-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-vrykounta-olympo-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis\, Vrykounta (Olympos)
LOCATION:Olympos / Vrykounta\, Karpathos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 28-29 August the people of Olympos walk down to the underground church of Agios Ioannis at Vrykounta\, an ancient site on the far north coast: park at Avlona and walk about 90 minutes down the old path\, carrying a sleeping bag because everyone spends the night on the stone terraces around the church. Braised goat\, chickpea soup and loukoumades are served at long tables\, and the mantinades and dancing to lyra go on until dawn. Pack water and a torch\; there is only a small canteen.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/karpathos/#olympos-vrykounta-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-vrykounta-olympo
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/karpathos/#olympos-vrykounta-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-vrykounta-olympo
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kos-mastichari-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-mastichari-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Prodromos\, Mastichari
LOCATION:Mastichari\, Kos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Mastichari\, the ferry port for Kalymnos\, feasts the Beheading of St John on the evening of 28 August with live music and dancing by the harbour. It also holds a wine festival in the first week of August.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kos/#mastichari-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-mastichari
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kos/#mastichari-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-mastichari
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kythnos-dryopida-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-dryopida-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Prodromos\, Dryopida
LOCATION:Dryopida\, Kythnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Beheading of St John closes Dryopida's summer: vespers at the Prodromos church on the evening of 28 August and a glenti with the village's violin and laouto players\; the Prodromos in Chora and the chapel of Ai-Giannis tou Skylou celebrate the same night. As it's a strict fast day\, the food is Lenten — expect chickpeas\, olives and fava rather than meat.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#dryopida-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-dryopida
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#dryopida-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-dryopida
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lefkada-agios-ioannis-beach-lefkada-town-feast-of-agios-ioannis-antz-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Ioannis Antzousis\, Lefkada town
LOCATION:Agios Ioannis beach\, Lefkada town\, Lefkada\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The tiny chapel of Agios Ioannis Antzousis on the beach west of town\, said to have been founded by Angevin crusaders\, opens only for its feast: vespers on the evening of 28 August and liturgy on the 29th (Beheading of St John)\, with the town's families walking or cycling out along the lagoon. No big panigiri\, but a nice evening if you are staying in town\; the beach bars behind the chapel stay open.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lefkada/#agios-ioannis-beach-lefkada-town-feast-of-agios-ioannis-antz
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lefkada/#agios-ioannis-beach-lefkada-town-feast-of-agios-ioannis-antz
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:naxos-apeiranthos-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-apeiranthos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Prodromos\, Apeiranthos
LOCATION:Apeiranthos\, Naxos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:For the Beheading of St John on 29 August\, Apeiranthos feasts on the evening of the 28th with traditional dishes such as paspalas and sourdough bread\, wine\, and violin music and dancing in the square. Apollonas and Agersani hold St John feasts the same night\, and Apeiranthos celebrates St John the Theologian again on 26 September.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#apeiranthos-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-apeiranthos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#apeiranthos-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-apeiranthos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:paros-lefkes-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-kaparos-lefkes-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Kaparos\, Lefkes
LOCATION:Lefkes\, Paros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Lefkes' second big night: on 28-29 August\, for the Beheading of St John\, the village feasts at the chapel of Ai-Giannis Kaparos with food from the association\, wine and violin-laouto dancing in the square. The same evening the monastery of Agios Ioannis Detis in the Paros Park at Kolymbithres holds its vespers\, so some people do both. The village is pedestrian\; park at the top by the bus stop.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#lefkes-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-kaparos-lefkes
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#lefkes-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-kaparos-lefkes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sifnos-faros-panigiri-of-ai-giannis-nistevtis-faros-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Ai-Giannis Nistevtis\, Faros
LOCATION:Faros\, Sifnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:For the Beheading of St John (29 August) Sifnos has five Ai-Giannis feasts on the evening of the 28th — Choni\, Mavro Chorio\, Siderou\, Mangana — but the easiest for visitors is Ai-Giannis 'the Faster' at Faros\, a chapel above the beach\, which does its panigiri on the morning of the 29th after liturgy. Being a fast day\, the panigyras serves the Lenten menu: cod with cabbage salad instead of lamb\, alongside the revithada.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#faros-panigiri-of-ai-giannis-nistevtis-faros
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#faros-panigiri-of-ai-giannis-nistevtis-faros
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:syros-alithini-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-alithini-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Prodromos\, Alithini
LOCATION:Alithini\, Syros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Alithini\, the village on the hill just outside Ermoupoli\, keeps the Beheading of St John on 28-29 August with vespers and a glenti with food\, wine and music. The same village also feasts Agia Anna and Agia Paraskevi on 26 July. Poseidonia on the south coast holds a St John panigiri the same night.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/syros/#alithini-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-alithini
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/syros/#alithini-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-prodromos-alithini
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fournoi-agios-ioannis-thermastis-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-thermasti-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270829
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Thermastis
LOCATION:Agios Ioannis Thermastis\, Fournoi\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:At the chapel of St John in the rural settlement of Thermastis\, 7 km from the port\, the church committee marks the Beheading of the Forerunner with liturgy\, refreshments and\, in the evening\, souvlaki\, mezedes and a live traditional band in the chapel square. The fireworks-and-Easter-decoration team (PKF) also uses the same chapel for a fundraising panigiri a couple of weeks earlier (17 August in 2025). Dirt road at the end\; a lift from a local is the usual way in.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/fournoi/#agios-ioannis-thermastis-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-thermasti
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/fournoi/#agios-ioannis-thermastis-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-thermasti
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-mavrato-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-nistevtis-mavrato-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270829
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Nistevtis\, Mavrato
LOCATION:Mavrato\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Mavrato\, a farming village in the hills west of Agios Kirykos\, marks the Beheading of St John on 29 August with a panigiri that runs 'from midday until morning': roast kid\, boiled goat\, octopus pilaf and mezedes\, with Nikos Fakaros's orchestra in 2024. One of the last chances of the season to dance the ikariotikos\; Proespera in Raches keeps the same saint the same day.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#mavrato-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-nistevtis-mavrato
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#mavrato-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-nistevtis-mavrato
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-proespera-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-nistevtis-proespera-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270829
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270830
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Nistevtis\, Proespera
LOCATION:Proespera\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Proespera\, a hamlet on the Raches plateau\, closes the west-coast season on 29 August with local meat\, mezedes and plenty of wine\, the Zevkalides playing in 2025. Small and friendly\; it is the Raches-side twin of the Mavrato feast the same day.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#proespera-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-nistevtis-proespera
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#proespera-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-nistevtis-proespera
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sifnos-agios-symeon-hill-kamares-panigiri-of-agios-symeon-summit-ch-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270902
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Symeon (summit chapel)\, above Kamares
LOCATION:Agios Symeon hill (Kamares)\, Sifnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The end-of-summer feast on the 476 m peak of Agios Symeon above Kamares: on the evening of 31 August people walk or drive up the track for vespers\, then eat revithada and lamb at the monastery's long tables with a violin-laouto takimi. The chapel of Pantokratoras at the Platys Gialos–Chrysopigi junction celebrates the same night and is the easy-access alternative. Ask at your hotel whether the panigyras is laying on food that year — it depends on the sponsor.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#agios-symeon-hill-kamares-panigiri-of-agios-symeon-summit-ch
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#agios-symeon-hill-kamares-panigiri-of-agios-symeon-summit-ch
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
